-- Spanish 1 course record. Safe to run more than once.
alter table public.courses add column if not exists video_url text;

insert into public.courses (slug, title, subject, credits, focus)
values ('spanish-1', 'Spanish 1', 'Electives', 1.0, $j$Spanish 1 is a one credit world language course that helps students begin to read, write, speak and understand Spanish while learning to love and serve neighbors of every nation. Students study the Spanish alphabet and pronunciation, greetings and courtesy, introductions, numbers, days, months and dates, family, nouns, articles and adjectives, the verbs ser, estar and tener, school vocabulary, regular present tense verbs, telling time, food and the verb gustar, stem changing verbs, shopping, places in town, the verb ir and directions, the home, the body and health vocabulary, weather and hobbies, the Spanish speaking world and Hispanic Florida, church and faith vocabulary, future plans, an introduction to the past tense and serving others with Spanish. Each lesson connects to Scripture in the King James Version, and all Scripture quotations in the course are in the King James Version. The course includes six units, lesson checks, unit quizzes, assessments, discussions and a final portfolio and exam. Students practice reading, writing, listening and speaking, and learn about the cultures of Spanish speaking peoples with respect.$j$)
on conflict (slug) do nothing;
